  _isSmallIngredient: 0
  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: Whispers in the lowly streets of Verehn tell of
    an old tale. A nobleman with a tall hat found a peasant mixing a barrel of potato
    batter with his pitchfork. When offered to try some, the nobleman agreed. The
    taste was of such sweetness that even the sky turned blue, for the Sun barged
    past the clouds to try the batter for itself. The nobleman desired that all try
    the peasant's batter, and created the steam-powered blender. Thus began the Industrial
    Revolution and the culinary legacy of Verehn.
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: Boil them, mash them, stick them in a stew. The
    potato is the common meal for the common man. Conquest from the early Moshchnyy
    weaponized starvation and sacks of green potatoes to poison adversaries further
    out on the frontier. For every thousand dead men, the empire stretched two thousand
    kilometers further east. The Green Reaper now rests in your cupboards. For whom
    will its bell toll?
